{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229885-stitched-flesh-artifacts","id":1229885,"title":"Stitched Flesh Artifacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-24T17:16:02-07:00","id":1229885,"title":"Stitched Flesh Artifacts","content":"I've been working on an update of Ghosts to 3e and I recently recalled something from the 2e write-up for Thorns. There's a nemissary in the court of Thorns that wears as his physical body the Patchwork Regalia, which is a corpse made from the best parts of all the Dragon-Blooded slaughtered during the conquest of the city. It struck me that this sort of story is in much the same vein as the origin stories of artifacts from Arms of the Chosen and it might be interesting for such a thing to be an artifact with Evocations, perhaps allowing the possessing nemissary to learn powers that approximate some of the abilities of the Dragon-Blooded. Of course, such an artifact has other problems. Since such an artifact couldn't have the near-invulnerability to damage that most artifacts have, how would you go about ensuring that a ghost player that has such a thing can reasonably maintain his character investment in it? What other variations of such artifacts would you also expect to see?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T18:07:39-07:00","id":1229894,"title":"","content":"I had forgotten about that little detail. Is it me, or does that sound a lot like a Liminal?<br /> <br /> Regardless if you go the Artifact route, the invulnerability aspect is easily dealt with; it is remarkably easier to repair (allowing a simple Craft or Medicine roll for the attuned to repair it; no special Occult or Craft: Artifact required). You could even tie this into the Evocations; the number of which you have unlocked doesn't change but the particulars may vary based on who you used as parts. Currently it would allow the nemissary a bunch of faux elemental effects based on the Dragonblood but if it gets damaged it might lose some of them temporarily and if you repair it using parts from a Lunar you might get back different Evocations, relating to the Lunar's totem or shapeshifting instead. If the attuned does have the special skills for Artifact repair or is willing to spend craft xp of the right grade, then maybe you can pick which part of the dead donor becomes the new Evocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T03:24:35-07:00","id":1234227,"title":"","content":"In previous editions, these were called Transcendent Revenant Vessels, and were built with a point-buy system where you allocated points into either the base attributes of the corpse (physical and I think Appearance, as rest is up to the Nemissary) or special features like implanted armor/weapons, horrible stench, illusion of life and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}